    {
      "id": "daedalus-journey",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "FROM IMAGE EXPERIMENT TO WORLD",
      "body": "Daedalus began as Estafos & Suraya, a practical question about early generative-image tools: could a very small team turn unstable source images into a coherent narrative work instead of a folder of disconnected experiments?\n\nThe answer became a science-fiction story about two people who meet by accident on a planet that has trapped them, then discover that the mystery—and their own histories—are connected. I wrote and designed the 12-page comic, assembled and standardized the generated source material, built the pages in Figma, animated panels in Rive and helped turn the work into an interactive reader. The world later expanded into its own website, identity, merchandise and live-action film work.",
      "source": "",
      "mediaRef": "",
      "href": "",
      "label": "",
      "projectId": "",
      "alt": "",
      "fit": "cover"
    },
