    {
      "id": "daedalus-process",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "PROCESS",
      "body": "Story and script → generated source images → selection and cleanup → page design in Figma → panel animation in Rive → reader state machine and JavaScript progression. The difficult part was not producing images; it was forcing many imperfect inputs to behave like one authored world.",
      "source": "",
      "mediaRef": "",
      "href": "",
      "label": "",
      "projectId": "",
      "alt": "",
      "fit": "cover"
    },
    {
      "id": "daedalus-reception",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "SAME PROJECT, RADICALLY DIFFERENT ENTRY POINTS",
      "body": "A process-led post about creating the world, story, comic and animation in two months reached 9K views. A later post led with the personal reason for making the comic and reached 2.0M views, 3,417 upvotes and 236 comments. The work did not suddenly become two hundred times better; the framing gave people a human reason to enter it. That lesson now sits beside the production process because presenting a project is part of designing how it is understood.",
      "source": "",
      "mediaRef": "",
      "href": "",
      "label": "",
      "projectId": "",
      "alt": "",
      "fit": "cover"
    },
